Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?=EF=BB=BFRun=20the=20SPU=20side=20of=20SPURS=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?natively?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The kernel, system service, taskset and job chain policy modules are native C with the firmware's guest-visible behaviour: workload selection and contention, the kernel LS context, taskset requests, syscalls and context switches, and job chain command processing with the firmware's DMA order. SPUs serialize on a job chain with a host lock instead of spinning on its lock byte through GETLLAR/PUTLLC; idle SPUs block on the lock-line reservation. The lifted firmware SPU bodies, their stack-reset registry and the related lifter paths are removed; only the codec .pic plugins are still lifted.
